BOUNDARY: This detects persistent redirector/type/device/inode drift between child admission and the immediate pre-scan observation. It does not close replacement after revalidation but before `scandir`, swap-and-restore, or identity reuse. A stronger platform-specific handle-binding strategy would be a separate proposal, not silently implied by this patch.
